              "definition": "Allowing only one thread at a time to hold a lock-protected section."
            },
            {
              "term": "critical section",
              "definition": "Code that accesses shared state and must not be interleaved unsafely with competing threads."
            },
            {
              "term": "race condition",
              "definition": "A bug where the result depends on unpredictable timing or interleaving between concurrent operations."
            }
